Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 16:06:48 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 23/24] Runner: the results' tags in the font of the game's
 names

Gibax: the tags on the results screen should look like the game's names
(KNUCKLES...), not like our pixel font.

The runner reads "GoalResult_01_E" in the loaded GTSE (nothing of the
game in this source) and takes the letters its names have: a letter is
the k-th piece of strong fill of a name with the texels nearest to it,
its outline completed by a generated one with the game's profile. The
letters the names lack (B F P Q X Z, 2-9, ! ? _) are fills rendered from
a TTF Gibax gave (DejaVu Sans Bold Oblique renamed, Bitstream Vera
licence) at the names' size. A tag is laid out like the names (fills one
texel apart, the strongest index wins where letters touch), centred like
them, in its racer's 16-row band of a third texture of the block
(version 5 of the srnp_etiquettes file mod, 128x128 C4, the names'
palette copied in).

The results' routine (41 words) binds that texture and draws the name's
cell 2 units shorter at the top and bottom; its entry and band table
follow it in the same padding (0x800050E0, 0x80005120).

Measured (2 runners, 8 seats, phase 2 runner + this code, the 8 racers
CPUs, SRNP_TAGS=GIBAX,,K-NUX,AMY_R,,WAVE!,BOB-PIP,TAILSMKR): the v5 GTSE
loads; 8 finishes, 201 checksums equal, 2 divergences in camera fields;
the runner's texture is the prototype's (work\etiquettes\
police_resultats.py) texel for texel in all 8 bands; the results show
TAILSMKR, BOB-PIP, GIBAX in the names' font next to NIGHTS.

